Subject: [M156] [maglev] Validate alternative type checks before reusing
 conversions

Original change's description:
> [maglev] Validate alternative type checks before reusing conversions
>
> MaglevGraphOptimizer could replace a conversion node with a cached
> alternative that performed a weaker type check. For example, a
> TruncateCheckedNumberOrOddballToInt32 assuming kNumber could be replaced
> by a cached alternative assuming kNumberOrOddball. This dropped the
> stricter deopt guard, allowing non-Numbers (such as Booleans) to reach
> downstream operations that rely on the stronger type.
>
> This CL introduces a check ensuring that an alternative can only be
> reused if its guaranteed input type satisfies the requested input type.
>
> Fixed: 567129324
> Change-Id: I7909cce03bea404a9fc145e86ff5f9096a6a6964
> Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/v8/v8/+/8492751
